<h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
<p>We collect information in the following categories:</p>

<h3>Information you provide directly</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Account information:</strong> Name, email address, company name, and password when you register</li>
  <li><strong>Billing information:</strong> Payment method details (processed securely; we never store card data on our servers)</li>
  <li><strong>Content data:</strong> Text, keywords, URLs, images, and other content you submit for processing through our services</li>
  <li><strong>Communication data:</strong> Messages you send to our support team or through feedback channels</li>
</ul>

<h3>Information from social networks you connect</h3>
<p>If you connect a Facebook Page or an Instagram professional account to 1Platform, Meta shares with us, for the Pages and accounts you select and only with the permissions you approve:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Account identifiers:</strong> the ID, name, username and profile picture link of each Facebook Page and linked Instagram professional account you connect</li>
  <li><strong>Access credentials:</strong> the access tokens Meta issues for that connection, stored encrypted</li>
  <li><strong>Posts:</strong> the posts you publish through 1Platform and their identifiers, links and publishing status</li>
  <li><strong>Comments:</strong> comments people leave on those Pages and accounts, including the commenter's public name, their identifier on the network and the comment text, so you can read, reply to and hide them from your dashboard</li>
  <li><strong>Insights:</strong> aggregated metrics Meta reports for your Pages, accounts and posts, such as followers, reach, views, reactions, comments and shares</li>
</ul>

<h3>Information collected automatically</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Usage data:</strong> API calls, feature usage, timestamps, and session duration</li>
  <li><strong>Device information:</strong> Browser type, operating system, screen resolution, and device identifiers</li>
  <li><strong>Log data:</strong> IP addresses, referring URLs, pages visited, and error logs</li>
  <li><strong>Cookies and similar technologies:</strong> As described in our <a href={l('/cookies/')}>Cookie Policy</a></li>
</ul>

<h2>2. How We Use Your Information</h2>
<p>We use your information to:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Provide, maintain, and improve the Service</li>
  <li>Process transactions and send related information (confirmations, invoices)</li>
  <li>Send technical notices, updates, security alerts, and support messages</li>
  <li>Respond to your comments, questions, and support requests</li>
  <li>Monitor and analyze usage trends to improve user experience</li>
  <li>Detect, investigate, and prevent fraudulent or unauthorized activity</li>
  <li>Comply with legal obligations</li>
</ul>
<p>Data from social networks you connect is used only to publish the content you schedule, show you the comments on your Pages and accounts so you can reply to or hide them, and report your performance. We do not use it for advertising, we do not sell it, and we do not combine it across different businesses.</p>

<h2>3. Data Sharing and Third-Party Providers</h2>
<p>To deliver our unified platform capabilities, we share specific categories of data with the following third-party service providers:</p>

<h3>AI processing providers</h3>
<p>We use <strong>OpenAI</strong> for AI-powered content generation, comment creation, and text processing. Content you submit for AI processing (keywords, prompts, article parameters) is sent to OpenAI's API for processing. OpenAI's data usage policies apply to this processing.</p>

<h3>Search engine APIs</h3>
<p>We use <strong>ValueSerp</strong> to retrieve search engine results data for keyword research and SERP analysis. Search queries and keyword data are transmitted to ValueSerp for processing.</p>

<h3>Search data providers</h3>
<p>Search volume, keyword difficulty, and related keyword data may be sourced through third-party search data APIs to provide comprehensive keyword intelligence.</p>

<h3>Image sourcing providers</h3>
<p>We use <strong>Pixabay</strong> and <strong>Pexels</strong> to source royalty-free images for your content. Search queries related to image requests are transmitted to these providers.</p>

<h3>Link building providers</h3>
<p>We use <strong>Publisuites</strong> for link building and sponsored content placement services. Website URLs, anchor text, and campaign parameters are shared as necessary to execute link building campaigns.</p>

<h3>Payment processors</h3>
<p>We use <strong>Migo</strong> as our payment processing provider in Guatemala. When you make a payment, your transaction details (amount, currency, payment method) are securely transmitted to Migo for processing. We never store your complete credit card information on our servers.</p>

<h3>Invoicing providers</h3>
<p>We use <strong>TribuTax</strong> as our electronic invoicing (FEL) provider for generating legally compliant invoices in Guatemala. Your billing information (name, tax ID, address) is shared with TribuTax to generate and certify electronic invoices as required by Guatemalan tax law.</p>

<h3>Delivery and courier providers</h3>
<p>When you dispatch an order through a contracted courier service rather than your own staff, the delivery details you supply are transmitted to that courier so it can collect and deliver the parcel: your buyer's name, phone number, delivery address and, where you provide them, its coordinates. Deliveries you fulfil with your own staff are not shared with anyone. The public tracking link your buyer opens identifies the shipment and does not disclose the courier.</p>

<h3>Social networks</h3>
<p>When you connect a Facebook Page or an Instagram professional account, we exchange data with <strong>Meta Platforms</strong> on your behalf: we send the posts you publish and the replies you write, and we receive the data described in section 1. Meta's terms and data policy apply to that content on its platforms.</p>

<h3>Advertising networks</h3>
<p>If you connect an advertising account to run paid campaigns, you grant us management scopes over the pages and campaigns you select on that network so we can publish and control them on your behalf. The campaign material you create, the budget you assign and the performance figures the network reports back are exchanged with that network. This happens only for accounts you connect yourself, and we never sell your data to advertisers.</p>

<h3>Card-present acquiring providers</h3>
<p>If you request a terminal to accept card-present payments, the supporting documentation you upload is shared with the acquiring provider that reviews the request: your business's legal documents and its tax identification. The provider uses them to assess and resolve your request and retains them as financial regulation requires.</p>

<h3>Other sharing</h3>
<p>We may also share your information:</p>
<ul>
  <li>When required by law, regulation, or legal process</li>
  <li>To protect the rights, property, or safety of 1Platform Labs, our users, or the public</li>
  <li>In connection with a merger, acquisition, or sale of assets (with prior notice)</li>
  <li>With your consent or at your direction</li>
</ul>

<h2>4. Data Storage and Security</h2>
<p>Your data is stored on secure servers with industry-standard protections, including:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Encryption in transit (TLS 1.2+) and at rest</li>
  <li>Token-based authentication with role separation</li>
  <li>Regular security audits and vulnerability assessments</li>
  <li>Access controls limiting data access to authorized personnel only</li>
</ul>
<p>While we implement robust security measures, no method of electronic transmission or storage is 100% secure. We cannot guarantee absolute security of your data.</p>

<h2>5. Data Retention</h2>
<p>We retain your data according to the following schedule:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Account data:</strong> Retained while your account is active and for 30 days after deletion</li>
  <li><strong>Generated content:</strong> Retained for up to 90 days after account deletion</li>
  <li><strong>API logs:</strong> Retained for 90 days for debugging and analytics</li>
  <li><strong>Billing records:</strong> Retained as required by applicable tax and accounting laws</li>
  <li><strong>Social network credentials:</strong> Deleted automatically after you disconnect a Page or account, within 24 hours once no other Page or account connected with the same authorization remains. If the authorization expires or is revoked in Meta, the credentials stop working and the Page or account is marked for reconnection; they are deleted when you disconnect it or ask us to delete your data</li>
  <li><strong>Social network comments:</strong> Kept while the Page or account is connected, and deleted 90 days after you disconnect it, or earlier on request</li>
  <li><strong>Social network insights:</strong> Retained for up to 16 months to show period comparisons, and deleted earlier when you ask us to delete your account</li>
  <li><strong>Anonymized analytics:</strong> May be retained indefinitely in aggregate form</li>
</ul>

<h2>6. Your Rights</h2>
<p>Depending on your jurisdiction, you may have the following rights regarding your personal data:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Access:</strong> Request a copy of the personal data we hold about you</li>
  <li><strong>Correction:</strong> Request correction of inaccurate or incomplete data</li>
  <li><strong>Deletion:</strong> Request deletion of your personal data (subject to legal retention requirements)</li>
  <li><strong>Portability:</strong> Request your data in a structured, machine-readable format</li>
  <li><strong>Objection:</strong> Object to processing of your data for certain purposes</li>
  <li><strong>Restriction:</strong> Request restriction of processing in certain circumstances</li>
</ul>
<p>To exercise any of these rights, contact us at <strong>privacy@1platform.pro</strong>. We will respond to your request within 30 days.</p>

<h2 id="data-deletion">7. Data Deletion Instructions</h2>
<p>You can ask us to delete your personal data at any time. This includes the data we receive from Meta when a business connects its WhatsApp Business account, a Facebook Page or an Instagram professional account to 1Platform: the identifiers of those accounts and phone numbers, the access credentials issued for each connection, the conversations and contact details exchanged with the business's customers, and the posts, comments and insights of the connected Pages and accounts.</p>

<h3>If you are a business using 1Platform</h3>
<ol>
  <li>To stop us from receiving and sending WhatsApp messages for your number, switch the channel off in your dashboard under <strong>Sales &rsaquo; Channels</strong>, or remove 1Platform from the apps connected to your business portfolio in Meta Business Suite.</li>
  <li>To stop us from publishing to or reading a Facebook Page or Instagram account, open <strong>Social media &rsaquo; Accounts</strong> in your dashboard and choose <strong>Disconnect</strong>; its access credentials are then deleted automatically. To also withdraw the permission in Meta, remove 1Platform under <strong>Settings &rsaquo; Business integrations</strong> in Facebook.</li>
  <li>To have your account and its data deleted, email <strong>privacy@1platform.pro</strong> from the email address of your account, with the subject <strong>&ldquo;Data deletion request&rdquo;</strong>.</li>
</ol>

<h3>If you wrote to a business that uses 1Platform</h3>
<p>Email <strong>privacy@1platform.pro</strong> with the subject <strong>&ldquo;Data deletion request&rdquo;</strong>, the name of the business you wrote to and the phone number you used, or the Facebook or Instagram profile you commented from. We process those conversations and comments on behalf of that business, so we coordinate the deletion with it.</p>

<h3>What happens after your request</h3>
<ul>
  <li>We reply within 30 days and confirm when the deletion is complete.</li>
  <li>We delete your account data, the credentials of any connected channel or social account, the stored conversations and contact details, and the stored comments and insights.</li>
  <li>Records we are required by law to keep, such as invoices and tax records, are retained only for the period the law requires and then deleted.</li>
</ul>

<h2>8. Cookies</h2>
<p>We use cookies and similar tracking technologies to enhance your experience. For detailed information about the cookies we use and how to manage them, please see our <a href={l('/cookies/')}>Cookie Policy</a>.</p>

<h2>9. Children's Privacy</h2>
<p>The Service is not directed to individuals under 18 years of age. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If we become aware that we have collected personal data from a child without parental consent, we will take steps to delete that information promptly.</p>

<h2>10. International Data Transfers</h2>
<p>Your data may be transferred to and processed in countries other than your country of residence. When we transfer data internationally, we ensure appropriate safeguards are in place to protect your information in accordance with this Privacy Policy.</p>

<h2>11. Changes to This Policy</h2>
<p>We may update this Privacy Policy periodically. We will notify you of material changes by posting the updated policy on our website and updating the "Last updated" date. Your continued use of the Service after changes take effect constitutes acceptance of the revised policy.</p>

<h2>12. Contact Information</h2>
<p>If you have questions or concerns about this Privacy Policy or our data practices, please contact us:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Email:</strong> privacy@1platform.pro</li>
  <li><strong>Website:</strong> <a href="https://1platform.pro">https://1platform.pro</a></li>
</ul>
